{"aggregate_id": "01KZ0SRBTBFDRFM0MVT62AEVB4", "aggregate_type": "Mission", "event_id": "01KZ0SRCC0GQH7B8N4GPTFA9BA", "event_type": "MissionCreated", "payload": {"created_at": "2026-08-02T08:34:26.253790+00:00", "friendly_name": "Doctrine-Charter Split: Single-Path Authority Foundation", "mission_id": "01KZ0SRBTBFDRFM0MVT62AEVB4", "mission_number": null, "mission_slug": "doctrine-charter-split-unification-01KZ0SRB", "mission_type": "software-dev", "purpose_context": "Follow-up to #3146. The compiled charter.yaml is the deterministic, schema-guarded resolution authority and takes precedence; charter.md is demoted to a secondary rationale/prose read point. This mission retires the residual charter.md presence/config readers that survived #3146 (dashboard #3150, analysis_report, the charter/context OR-gate, and the retrospective-policy frontmatter resolver), unifies the meta.json fail-closed authority (#3140), deletes the one real upward layer edge, folds cheap surface-cleaners (#3149 CI path filter, #3107 inert parity gate, #3102 closeout), and lays the wheel packaging-closure groundwork (mint spec-kitty-kernel pyproject, fix the doctrine pyproject + closure test, charter-wheel assessment/ADR). The #3101 kernel->doctrine->charter wheel cutover is a deferred, explicit follow-on.", "purpose_tldr": "Make the doctrine-pack & charter split usable by resting it on ONE charter read/path authority (charter.yaml) with correct kernel<-doctrine<-charter<-glossary/runtime<-specify_cli wiring; the wheel cutover is a sequenced follow-on.", "target_branch": "feat/doctrine-charter-split-unification", "wp_count": 0}, "project_slug": "spec-kitty", "project_uuid": "8a4a7da6-a97c-4bb4-893a-b31664abfee4", "schema_version": "5.0.0", "timestamp": "2026-08-02T08:34:26.816650+00:00"}
